 "commit_18798852": [
  "18798852cbe825498fba55e40be4a279a1eb6243",
  "Andrei Mihai Visalon",
  "Tue Aug 11 05:09:42 2026 +0300",
  "feat(command-center): measure the two no-remote repos - 77 files, 735 KB, exist nowhere else",
  "A git-hygiene hook warned that `chk` and `scratch` under source/_advver_M14/ hold work that \"exists",
  "nowhere else\". Both are working copies of this toolchain, so that is a claim about UNIQUENESS and it",
  "is testable rather than something to act on directly. The owner standing decision for no-remote",
  "repos is TRIAGE FIRST - explicitly do not create remotes, do not push - so this measures and reports",
  "and changes nothing anywhere.",
  "MEASURED by content, LF-normalised, against every tracked blob in ast-integrate:",
  "    chk       7,770 files | 350 VARIANT | 77 ORPHAN",
  "    scratch   7,772 files | 348 VARIANT | 77 ORPHAN",
  "VARIANT means the same relative path EXISTS in the repo and the contents differ - a diverged copy of",
  "something already in version control, low risk. ORPHAN means no file at that path anywhere - the",
  "only copy. Only the second is work at risk, and conflating them is how a triage produces a scary",
  "number that means nothing.",
  "THE 77 ORPHANS ARE WHOLE SUBSYSTEMS, 735,139 bytes:",
  "    46  tools/web/agentify-desktop",
  "    17  tools/mcp/codex-orchestrator   (package.json, src/, integrations/codex/, manager/, orchestrator/)",
  "     7  tools/web/promptbridge-talk-lane",
  "     3  tools/mcp/agent-lanes-codex",
  "     2  tools/web/agent-lanes-chatgpt-web",
  "     2  root mcp-server.mjs + docs/incubating/tools/agentify-web-chatgpt-bridge.md",
  "chk at least has them in local git. scratch has ZERO commits, so its copies are working-tree files",
  "only: deleting that directory destroys them with no recovery. The decision - live work worth a",
  "remote, or abandoned experiments worth deleting - is the owner call. I measured uniqueness only and",
  "did not read them for intent.",
  "TWO DEFECTS IN MY OWN PROBE, both caught and both worth recording.",
  "First run appeared to hang for 30 minutes and emitted nothing. It was DEAD, not slow, and the design",
  "was the reason: I had written a `rev-list --objects --all` pass piping up to 20,000 shas through",
  "`cat-file --batch`, capturing the entire stream in memory and then DISCARDING it - the digests were",
  "never extracted. Minutes and gigabytes to contribute exactly nothing. Removed. Dropping it makes the",
  "comparison worktree-only, which is strictly MORE conservative: a file living only in deleted history",
  "now reports as unique rather than being silently cleared, and that is the safe direction of error",
  "for an is-this-at-risk question. The empty output was `| tail -32` buffering everything until exit",
  "and losing the pipe when the call was backgrounded; the rerun writes to a file instead.",
  "Second, the first working version reported \"427 unique files\". That was an OVERCLAIM - it counted",
  "modified copies of tracked files as unique. Adding the VARIANT/ORPHAN split took the real at-risk",
  "number from 427 to 77. The facts were right and the sentence was wider than the evidence, which is",
  "the same shape this program keeps finding in its own audits."
 ],
